{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1524031719,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzMTUzNDI5ODE=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2428","origin":"github"},"title":"Evaluate a potential merge of `add` and `save` into a single command","message":"This came up in #2043 \n\nWe should to do an assessment of the respective roles of add and save. Their functionality is massively overlapping with surprisingly different code paths. User-facing differences are: add has --to-git, while save has --version-tag, but that is about it.\n\nMy hunch is that we should merge the two into a single save command that largely behaves like the current add(save=True), but with the remaining features of save, namely: --version-tag and --all-updated=True. Power-users always have git add and git annex add at their disposal to achieve everything that save might be to blunt of an instrument for -- although I cannot yet see what would be missing...","files":null}]}